@startuml
title Dynamic Syntax Highlighting Workflow

actor User
participant "EditorViewController\n(View)" as View
participant "EditorViewModel\n(ViewModel)" as ViewModel
participant "AntlrGrammarService\n(Model)" as Antlr
participant "TokenHighlightMappingService" as Mapper

== 1. Grammar Loading ==
User -> View: Load Grammar
View -> ViewModel: loadGrammarAsync()
ViewModel -> View: DynamicGrammar loaded
View -> Mapper: buildVocabularyMapping(vocabulary)
activate Mapper
note right
  Pre-computes and caches CSS classes
  (keyword, operator, string, etc.)
  based on token rules.
end note
Mapper --> View
deactivate Mapper

== 2. Text Editing & Parsing ==
User -> View: Types text in CodeArea
View -> ViewModel: textContent property updated
activate ViewModel
ViewModel -> ViewModel: Debounce typing delay
ViewModel -> Antlr: parseText(dynamicGrammar, text)
activate Antlr
Antlr --> ViewModel: ParseResult (tokens, errors)
deactivate Antlr

ViewModel -> ViewModel: computeTokenStyles(tokens)
note right
  Calculates line-relative start/end
  bounds for each token.
end note
ViewModel -> View: tokens list updated (Event)
deactivate ViewModel

== 3. Rendering ==
activate View
View -> View: setSyntaxDecorator()
View -> View: createRichParagraph(paragraphIndex)

loop For each TokenStyle in current line
    View -> Mapper: getCssClass(tokenType)
    activate Mapper
    Mapper --> View: cssClass
    deactivate Mapper

    alt tokenText.startsWith("@")
        View -> View: override with "annotation"
    end

    View -> View: builder.addWithStyleNames(tokenText, cssClass)
end

View --> User: Displays styled text
deactivate View
@enduml
